# iCalendar mandates CRLF line endings (RFC 5545 §3.1), and the .ics files under
# testdata/ are byte-exact captures from real clients used as interop fixtures.
# Git's default eol normalisation would rewrite them to LF on checkout, silently
# invalidating what they exist to prove.
*.ics -text

# Golden wire-parity recordings (internal/dataentry/testdata/golden) are compared
# byte for byte, and the feed recordings carry iCalendar CRLF line endings.
*.golden -text
